        "thought_text": "Use dynamic programming to calculate the minimum number of recolors needed for each possible ending color at each position in the garland. Maintain a DP table where dp[i][color] represents the minimum number of recolors needed to reach position i with the lamp at position i being of color. Transition between states by considering the cost of recoloring or keeping the current color, ensuring the condition for a nice garland is met.",
